      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "program",
        "groupId": "6dbd64f7-4ce7-45f4-9b59-019916a1c43d",
        "position": 2,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p><strong>Fall&nbsp;2027&nbsp;Admission&nbsp;for&nbsp;this&nbsp;Major:</strong></p><p>Transfer&nbsp;students&nbsp;who&nbsp;select&nbsp;this&nbsp;major&nbsp;on&nbsp;their&nbsp;College&nbsp;of&nbsp;Letters&nbsp;and&nbsp;Science&nbsp;(L&amp;S)&nbsp;application&nbsp;and&nbsp;are&nbsp;offered&nbsp;admission&nbsp;to&nbsp;L&amp;S&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;directly&nbsp;admitted&nbsp;into&nbsp;this&nbsp;major.&nbsp;If&nbsp;you&nbsp;are&nbsp;interested&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;major,&nbsp;it&nbsp;is&nbsp;very&nbsp;important&nbsp;to&nbsp;select&nbsp;this&nbsp;major&nbsp;on&nbsp;your&nbsp;application,&nbsp;and&nbsp;complete&nbsp;as&nbsp;many&nbsp;lower-division&nbsp;major&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;as&nbsp;possible&nbsp;prior&nbsp;to&nbsp;transfer.&nbsp;See&nbsp;details&nbsp;on&nbsp;preparation&nbsp;for&nbsp;this&nbsp;major&nbsp;below.</p><p></p><p><strong>The&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Earth&nbsp;and&nbsp;Planetary&nbsp;Science&nbsp;(EPS)</strong>&nbsp;offers&nbsp;six&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;specializations&nbsp;leading&nbsp;to&nbsp;a&nbsp;B.A.&nbsp;degree&nbsp;in&nbsp;one&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;following&nbsp;specializations&nbsp;:</p><p>-&nbsp;Atmospheric&nbsp;Science;</p><p>-&nbsp;Environmental&nbsp;Earth&nbsp;Science;</p><p>-&nbsp;Geology;</p><p>-&nbsp;Geophysics;</p><p>-&nbsp;Marine&nbsp;Science;&nbsp;and</p><p>-&nbsp;Planetary&nbsp;Science.</p><p></p><p>The&nbsp;degree&nbsp;provides&nbsp;quantitative&nbsp;studies&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;earth&nbsp;and&nbsp;is&nbsp;an&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;program&nbsp;toward&nbsp;further&nbsp;studies&nbsp;in&nbsp;graduate&nbsp;school&nbsp;or&nbsp;for&nbsp;active&nbsp;roles&nbsp;in&nbsp;environmental&nbsp;decision&nbsp;making,&nbsp;teaching&nbsp;in&nbsp;high&nbsp;schools,&nbsp;and&nbsp;for&nbsp;job&nbsp;opportunities&nbsp;requiring&nbsp;a&nbsp;basic&nbsp;understanding&nbsp;of&nbsp;natural&nbsp;sciences.</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Minimum&nbsp;Admission&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;Earth&nbsp;and&nbsp;Planetary&nbsp;Science&nbsp;major</strong></p><p><strong>Complete&nbsp;the&nbsp;equivalent&nbsp;of:</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>Chemistry&nbsp;1A&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;1AL</li><li>EPS&nbsp;50</li><li>Math&nbsp;51</li><li>Math&nbsp;52</li><li>Physics&nbsp;7A&nbsp;</li><li>Physics&nbsp;7B&nbsp;</li></ul><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 16px;\">Strongly&nbsp;recommended&nbsp;prior&nbsp;to&nbsp;transfer</strong></p><p><strong>Complete&nbsp;the&nbsp;equivalent&nbsp;of&nbsp;additional&nbsp;courses&nbsp;required&nbsp;for&nbsp;specialization&nbsp;of&nbsp;interest:</strong></p><p></p><p>Atmospheric&nbsp;Science,&nbsp;Geophysics,&nbsp;and&nbsp;Planetary&nbsp;Science:</p><ul><li>Math&nbsp;53</li><li>Math&nbsp;54</li><li>Physics&nbsp;7C</li></ul><p></p><p>Marine&nbsp;Science:</p><ul><li>Biology&nbsp;1B</li><li>EPS&nbsp;82</li></ul><p></p><p>Environmental&nbsp;Earth&nbsp;Science:</p><ul><li>Biology&nbsp;1B</li></ul><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">For&nbsp;more&nbsp;information:</strong></p><p>Anna&nbsp;Atkinson,&nbsp;Undergraduate&nbsp;Major&nbsp;Advisor</p><p>Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Earth&nbsp;and&nbsp;Planetary&nbsp;Science</p><p><a href=\"mailto:epsua@berkeley.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">epsua@berkeley.edu</a></p><p><a href=\"https://eps.berkeley.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">https://eps.berkeley.edu</a></p>",
        "groupId": "6609913a-d280-4fa3-be74-01986124e261",
        "position": 3,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
        "content": "exam credit",
        "groupId": "455dbc51-17a9-4ec9-a9ee-019916a1c43d",
        "position": 4,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<p><strong>The&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Earth&nbsp;and&nbsp;Planetary&nbsp;Science&nbsp;accepts&nbsp;the&nbsp;following&nbsp;AP/IB&nbsp;exam&nbsp;scores&nbsp;and&nbsp;A-Level&nbsp;grades&nbsp;as&nbsp;course&nbsp;equivalencies&nbsp;for&nbsp;EPS&nbsp;specializations:</strong></p><p></p><p>AP&nbsp;Calc&nbsp;AB&nbsp;–&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;3,&nbsp;4,&nbsp;5&nbsp;for&nbsp;Math&nbsp;51</p><p>AP&nbsp;Calc&nbsp;BC&nbsp;–&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;3&nbsp;or&nbsp;4&nbsp;for&nbsp;Math&nbsp;51;&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;5&nbsp;for&nbsp;Math&nbsp;52</p><p>AP&nbsp;Chem&nbsp;–&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;3,&nbsp;4&nbsp;or&nbsp;5&nbsp;meets&nbsp;Chem&nbsp;1A&nbsp;and&nbsp;1AL;&nbsp;4&nbsp;or&nbsp;5&nbsp;meets&nbsp;Chem&nbsp;3A</p><p>AP&nbsp;Bio&nbsp;–&nbsp;score&nbsp;of&nbsp;4&nbsp;or&nbsp;5&nbsp;for&nbsp;Biology&nbsp;1A&nbsp;and&nbsp;1B</p><p>IB&nbsp;Math&nbsp;Higher&nbsp;Level&nbsp;(grades&nbsp;5,&nbsp;6&nbsp;or&nbsp;7)&nbsp;-&nbsp;Math&nbsp;51&nbsp;Equivalency</p><p>A-Level&nbsp;Math&nbsp;(grade&nbsp;of&nbsp;\"B\"&nbsp;or&nbsp;better&nbsp;-&nbsp;Math&nbsp;51&nbsp;Equivalency</p><p>A-Level&nbsp;Further&nbsp;Math&nbsp;(grade&nbsp;of&nbsp;\"B\"&nbsp;or&nbsp;better)&nbsp;-&nbsp;Math&nbsp;51&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Math&nbsp;52&nbsp;Equivalency</p><p></p><p><strong>Please&nbsp;note&nbsp;that&nbsp;each&nbsp;college/department&nbsp;may&nbsp;have&nbsp;different&nbsp;score&nbsp;requirements.</strong></p><p></p><p><strong>Questions?&nbsp;Contact</strong>&nbsp;<a href=\"mailto:epsua@berkeley.edu\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">epsua@berkeley.edu</a></p>",
